See also:

- https://stackoverflow.com/q/27535289/155423
- https://stackoverflow.com/q/50345139/155423

Note that this can be easily modified to _enumerate_, or return an integer location along with each value:
```
fn main() {
    for (i, dir) in Direction::iterator().enumerate() {
        println!("{:?}", (i, dir));
    }
}
```
which produces:
```
(0, North)
(1, South)
(2, East)
(3, West)
```
